urname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Neat</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Werner</surname><given-names>NY</given-names></name><name><surname>Montgomerie</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Sperm size of African cichlids in relation to sperm competition.</article-title><source>Behav Ecol</source><volume>12</volume><fpage>726</fpage><lpage>731</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000413-Anderson1"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Anderson</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Dixson</surname><given-names>AF</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Motility and midpiece in primates.</article-title><source>Nature</source><volume>416</volume><fpage>496</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11932733</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000413-Gage2"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gage</surname><given-names>MJG</given-names></name><name><surname>Freckleton</surname><given-names>RP</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Relative testis size and sperm morphometry across mammals: no evidence for an association between sperm competition and sperm length.</article-title><source>Proc R Soc Lond B</source><volume>270</volume><fpage>625</fpage><lpage>632</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000413-Byrne1"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Byrne</surname><given-names>PG</given-names></name><name><surname>Simmons</surname><given-names>LW</given-names></name><name><surname>Roberts</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Sperm competition and the evolution of gamete morphology in frogs.</article-title><source>Proc R Soc Lond B</source><volume>270</volume><fpage>2079</fpage><lpage>2086</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000413-Anderson2"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Anderson</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Nyholt</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Dixson</surname><given-names>AF</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Sperm competition and the evolution of sperm midpiece volume in mammals.</article-title><source>J Zool Lond</source><volume>267</volume><fpage>135</fpage><lpage>142</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000413-Immler1"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Immler</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Birkhead</surname><given-names>TR</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Sperm competition and sperm midpiece size: no consistent pattern in passerines.</article-title><source>Proc R Soc Lond B</source><volume>274</volume><fpage>561</fpage><lpage>568</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000413-Immler2"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Immler</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Moore</surname><given-names>ADM</given-names></name><name><surname>Breed</surname><given-names>WG</given-names></name><name><surname>Birkhead</surname><given-names>TR</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>By hook or by crook? Morphometry, competition and cooperation in rodent sperm.</article-title><source>PLoS ONE</source><volume>2</volume><fpage>e170</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17245446</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000413-Ward1"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ward</surname><given-names>PI</given-names></name></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Intraspecific variation in sperm size characters.</article-title><source>Heredity</source><volume>80</volume><fpage>655</fpage><lpage>659</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9675869</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000413-Morrow2"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Morrow</surname><given-names>EH</given-names></name><name><surname>Gage</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Consistent significant variation between individual males in spermatozoal morphometry.</article-title><source>J Zool Lond</source><volume>254</volume><fpage>147</fpage><lpage>153</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000413-Birkhead5"><label>25</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Birkhead</surname><given-names>TR</given-names></name><name><surname>Pellat</surname><given-names>EJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Brekke</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Yeates</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Castillo-Juarez</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Genetic effects on sperm design in the zebra finch.</article-title><source>Nature</source><volume>434</volume><fpage>383</fpage><lpage>387</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15772662</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000413-Parker1"><label>26</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Parker</surname><given-names>GA</given-names></name></person-group><year>1982</year><article-title>Why are there so many tiny sperm? Sperm competition and the maintenance of the two sexes.</article-title><source>J Theor Biol</source><volume>96</volume><fpage>281</fpage><lpage>294</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7121030</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000413-Parker2"><label>27</label><c